  "system": {
    "description": "<p>An improvised weapon is an object constructed for a function other than harm but nevertheless can cause injury. Examples include frying pans and broken bottles. When you use an improvised weapon to attack, you roll with 1 bane. On a critical success or critical failure, the improvised weapon breaks. An improvised weapon deals 1d6 damage. Reduce any Bonus Damage applied to the attack to 0.</p>",
